  "body": "All agents' buyers are welcomed. Contact Wayne and Emma for conjunction.\r\n\r\nTucked away in a quiet Half Moon Bay cul-de-sac, this inviting home is currently presented as four bedrooms, including the room presented as the primary bedroom, which is identified as a \"sewing room\" on Council-approved plans. With two bathrooms and a versatile layout, the home offers everyday comfort in a convenient location.\r\n\r\nWalk to Wakaaranga School and Farm Cove Intermediate, with zoning for Pigeon Mountain School and Pakuranga College. Half Moon Bay Marina, the ferry, coastal walkways, PAK'nSAVE and Highland Park are all just minutes away.\r\n\r\nKey features:\r\n- Currently presented as four bedrooms-the primary bedroom is identified as a \"sewing room\" on Council-approved plans\r\n- Two bathrooms\r\n- Garage space, part currently used as an office-see disclosure below\r\n- Peaceful cul-de-sac setting\r\n- Excellent school zones\r\n- Minutes to the marina, ferry and shops\r\n\r\nFrom the weekday school run to weekend coastal walks and ferry trips, enjoy a peaceful retreat close to the places that make everyday life convenient.\r\n\r\nPlease note: Council-approved plans identify the room currently presented as the primary bedroom as a \"sewing room\". Part of the garage is currently used as an office, with its consented use remaining as garage space. Purchasers are advised to undertake their own due diligence, review the Council property file and seek independent legal or building advice to satisfy themselves as to the compliance and lawful use of these areas, and their suitability for the purchasers' intended purposes.\r\n\r\nSpace, schools and lifestyle-this is Half Moon Bay living made easy.\r\n\r\nCall us for further information or visit a scheduled open home.",
